00:12:38.609 --> 00:12:40.808
Your two sons died
getting their heads shaved

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:41.996
at orientation.

00:12:42.202 --> 00:12:43.885
They didn't even make it
to the barracks.

00:12:43.962 --> 00:12:46.296
Oh, the cost of freedom!

00:12:46.315 --> 00:12:48.482
Here's a flag
we didn't bother to fold.

00:12:53.622 --> 00:12:55.739
I really want to thank you
for inviting me to dinner,

00:12:55.816 --> 00:12:57.132
Mr. and Mrs. Griffin.

00:12:57.134 --> 00:12:59.484
Hey, Nugget, you ever seen
that video of Fabio

00:12:59.561 --> 00:13:01.244
getting hit in the face
by a goose?

00:13:01.321 --> 00:13:03.413
-It's hilarious.
-Not for the goose.

00:13:03.438 --> 00:13:06.088
-She was killed.
-Oh, then that's doubly funny.

00:13:06.113 --> 00:13:08.538
Fabio's got a bloody nose
and a bird is dead.

00:13:08.645 --> 00:13:10.754
Mr. Griffin,
that goose had a name.

00:13:10.779 --> 00:13:13.130
It was Evelyn.
And she had 23 children.

00:13:13.306 --> 00:13:15.424
Here, let me show you
her GoFundMe page.

00:13:15.449 --> 00:13:16.927
What's your guys'
Wi-Fi password?

00:13:17.003 --> 00:13:20.822
It's "ChickensAreScum,"
and then 22 exclamation points.

00:13:20.824 --> 00:13:23.491
It's on the bulletin board
for when we Airbnb the house.

00:13:23.493 --> 00:13:26.103
Peter, we are not
Airbnb-ing the house.

00:13:26.179 --> 00:13:27.509
Eh, it might be too late
for that.

00:13:27.563 --> 00:13:29.713
Hey, is there any soap
in the upstairs bathroom?

00:13:29.833 --> 00:13:32.776
If you read the PDF, it said
you had to bring your own soap.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.554
Well, I'll just
use the shampoo as soap.

00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:36.596
He's a medical student.

00:13:36.673 --> 00:13:39.554
You know, you guys are being
very rude to my boyfriend.

00:13:39.579 --> 00:13:41.504
-I love him.
-I've had enough.

00:13:41.736 --> 00:13:43.816
Meg, I'm giving you
an old tomato.

00:13:44.348 --> 00:13:46.790
And a final demand
or statement of terms,

00:13:46.815 --> 00:13:49.148
the rejection of which
will result in retaliation

00:13:49.173 --> 00:13:50.765
or a permanent cessation
of relations.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.730
You either break up with him
or you break up with me.

00:13:53.755 --> 00:13:55.013
You can't date us both.

00:13:55.218 --> 00:13:56.835
Dad, you and I aren't dating.

00:13:56.957 --> 00:13:58.855
Oh, so you've made
your choice, then.

00:13:59.039 --> 00:14:00.575
Well, I'd like my tomato back.

00:14:02.366 --> 00:14:03.612
I'll pack my bags.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.561
What bags?
She literally owns nothing.

00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:13.268
Guys, before I go,
I have one thing to say.

00:14:13.409 --> 00:14:16.319
Is this a "pause The Last of Us"
type of conversation

00:14:16.344 --> 00:14:17.936
or can I "uh-huh"
my way through this?

00:14:17.961 --> 00:14:19.461
Peter, turn it off.

00:14:19.707 --> 00:14:22.642
If you don't accept Nugget,
you don't accept me.

00:14:22.719 --> 00:14:23.902
I'm moving in with him.

00:14:23.978 --> 00:14:25.720
You know what the British
are gonna call this?

00:14:25.799 --> 00:14:28.467
Megxit.
They're a clever little island.

00:14:28.492 --> 00:14:30.316
Meg, please don't go.

00:14:30.394 --> 00:14:31.484
You're my only daughter

00:14:31.561 --> 00:14:33.837
and I can't imagine
living without you.

00:14:33.966 --> 00:14:35.724
Plus, I need your vote
to keep a Billy Bass

00:14:35.771 --> 00:14:37.696
-out of our living room.
-I'm sorry, Mom.

00:14:37.751 --> 00:14:41.085
My decision has been made.
Goodbye.

00:14:41.139 --> 00:14:42.990
Well, now seems like
a good time

00:14:43.015 --> 00:14:44.497
to reopen the Billy Bass vote.

00:14:44.574 --> 00:14:45.929
All in favor, say aye.

00:14:46.049 --> 00:14:46.677
-Aye.
-Aye.
-Aye.

00:14:46.702 --> 00:14:48.351
-All opposed?
-Nay.

00:14:48.428 --> 00:14:49.519
-Present.
-Coward.

00:14:49.596 --> 00:14:51.396
Billy Bass approved.

00:14:53.158 --> 00:14:54.840
Billy, what do you think
Meg's gonna say

00:14:54.918 --> 00:14:55.919
to the Uber driver?

00:14:56.255 --> 00:14:58.773
Take me to the river

00:15:00.014 --> 00:15:02.348
Drop me in the water.

00:15:02.426 --> 00:15:04.476
Ah, we are thriving
without Meg.

00:15:10.934 --> 00:15:13.693
Is something wrong, Peter?
You've barely touched our food.

00:15:13.718 --> 00:15:16.219
I heard from Bonnie that
Meg moved out of the house

00:15:16.273 --> 00:15:17.897
and Lois could never breastfeed.

00:15:17.922 --> 00:15:19.346
What? How'd you hear that?

00:15:19.371 --> 00:15:20.884
Oh, Bonnie subscribes
to a service

00:15:20.961 --> 00:15:23.611
that alerts her any time
another mom fails.

00:15:23.613 --> 00:15:25.463
-That's wild.
-I know.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.148
Donna gives Cleveland Jr.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:28.950
unlimited
video game time, but...

00:15:29.253 --> 00:15:31.803
Peter, isn't it weird
with Meg out of the house?

00:15:31.856 --> 00:15:34.099
Nah, it's fine.
Although we got a lot more mice

00:15:34.124 --> 00:15:35.732
-around the house now.
-Mice?

00:15:35.809 --> 00:15:37.883
Yeah, Meg handled
all our rodent problems.

00:15:37.961 --> 00:15:40.219
She used to just squeeze 'em
and pop their heads off.

00:15:40.297 --> 00:15:42.313
All except one
that she'd leave alive

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.241
to run and go tell the story
to the others.

00:15:44.317 --> 00:15:45.520
Meg's a nice girl.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:47.068
Yeah, when I remodeled my house,

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.404
Meg hauled away
all the discarded insulation.

00:15:49.406 --> 00:15:50.405
Don't know what she did with it.

00:15:50.407 --> 00:15:51.906
Oh, yeah, Meg's great.

00:15:51.908 --> 00:15:54.409
She sold me a ton
of insulation super cheap.

00:15:54.411 --> 00:15:55.685
Oh, my God, you guys are right.

00:15:55.814 --> 00:15:58.073
This one time,
Meg fell down the stairs

00:15:58.098 --> 00:16:00.023
a-and she...
and-and she broke her clavicle.

00:16:04.022 --> 00:16:06.921
You guys, I think I miss Meg.

00:16:07.086 --> 00:16:10.758
Wa-Was there gonna be more
to the story about the stairs?

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.702
What do you say we go
to the giant chicken's house

00:16:12.779 --> 00:16:14.019
and get my daughter back?

00:16:14.343 --> 00:16:15.597
-I'm in.
-Let's do it.

00:16:15.599 --> 00:16:18.750
So the laughing was 'cause
your daughter hurt herself?

00:16:26.355 --> 00:16:28.960
Honey, did you order
a fat bag of crap?

00:16:29.036 --> 00:16:31.608
Stand aside. I'm here
to get my daughter back.

00:16:31.821 --> 00:16:33.245
She's not coming with you.

00:16:33.482 --> 00:16:35.499
-She's perfectly happy here.
-Are you sure?

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.413
We can make this
worth your while.

00:16:37.492 --> 00:16:39.431
We're prepared to trade
Brittney Griner.

00:16:39.611 --> 00:16:40.719
Hey, stop trading me.

00:16:40.794 --> 00:16:42.519
I just want to play basketball.

00:16:42.792 --> 00:16:44.383
And smoke weed, apparently.

00:16:44.461 --> 00:16:46.552
I wasn't smoking it,
I was just carrying it.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:48.905
Whatever. I'm still mad
we traded for you

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.632
instead of that other guy,
whose name

00:16:50.634 --> 00:16:52.721
I had never heard of
and can no longer remember.

00:16:52.811 --> 00:16:54.172
Yeah, that poor guy.

00:16:54.197 --> 00:16:55.780
Bring him home,
whatever his name is.

00:16:56.161 --> 00:16:57.897
Dad, what are you doing here?

00:16:57.974 --> 00:17:00.250
Meg, this nonsense has to stop.

00:17:00.326 --> 00:17:01.414
You're a Griffin, and...

00:17:01.998 --> 00:17:04.068
it's time to, uh... Do...

00:17:04.481 --> 00:17:06.481
do your neighbors
always have that bounce house

00:17:06.483 --> 00:17:08.574
or is this--
is it a special occasion?

00:17:08.652 --> 00:17:10.652
-I really don't know.
-Okay, yeah, but Meg,

00:17:10.654 --> 00:17:12.503
I mean it.
We all miss you, and--

00:17:12.528 --> 00:17:14.453
Oh, a heavy lady's
rolling into it.

00:17:14.478 --> 00:17:16.162
Probably the aunt
who likes to have fun.

00:17:16.678 --> 00:17:18.388
Wow, her face got red quick.

00:17:18.662 --> 00:17:20.678
Dad, I told you,
Nugget and his family

00:17:20.755 --> 00:17:22.664
treat me better
than you guys ever did.

00:17:22.666 --> 00:17:25.353
And I won't be coming home.
Dad?

00:17:26.149 --> 00:17:28.044
It's a Iron Man house!

00:17:28.864 --> 00:17:29.612
Okay, you know what,

00:17:29.689 --> 00:17:30.780
I think we need to regroup here.

00:17:30.782 --> 00:17:32.129
We're sorry
to have bothered you.

00:17:34.757 --> 00:17:36.043
I squashed a boy.

00:17:42.235 --> 00:17:45.219
Oh, come on, cheer up, Peter.
Look, the best thing to do

00:17:45.221 --> 00:17:47.054
to put all this
Meg drama behind us

00:17:47.056 --> 00:17:50.149
is a fun family activity
that we can all do together.

00:17:50.447 --> 00:17:52.502
You know, I was supposed
to be here today anyway,

00:17:52.578 --> 00:17:54.490
but then Tyler
cancelled his birthday party.

00:17:55.112 --> 00:17:58.431
Ice cream sundae bar
with Haribo brand gummi bears?

00:17:58.703 --> 00:18:01.629
Tyler! Tyler! Tyler!

00:18:01.921 --> 00:18:05.348
Hey, Ty. Guess we got
our wires crossed, huh?

00:18:07.976 --> 00:18:09.018
I-It was a numbers thing.

00:18:09.095 --> 00:18:11.688
I think his parents made him
invite the T-ball kids.

00:18:13.426 --> 00:18:15.484
- All right, Dad! Yeah!
- Good job, Giant Chicken!

00:18:15.509 --> 00:18:15.986
Yes!

00:18:16.586 --> 00:18:19.017
I've lost my daughter.

00:18:19.749 --> 00:18:20.887
Come on, gang.

00:18:20.912 --> 00:18:23.308
Group selfie for the family
Instagram account.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.860
Everybody say "seeds."

00:18:26.095 --> 00:18:27.823
Seeds!

00:18:32.555 --> 00:18:34.108
Griffin? What do you want?

00:18:34.437 --> 00:18:35.901
Um, I, uh...

00:18:36.389 --> 00:18:38.622
Meg, do you have
a flat dollar bill

00:18:38.699 --> 00:18:39.742
for the change machine?

00:18:39.838 --> 00:18:41.337
I wanted to play the arcades.

00:18:41.428 --> 00:18:43.553
-We don't play the arcades.
-Nerds.

00:18:43.629 --> 00:18:45.370
Because we have stand-up games

00:18:45.448 --> 00:18:47.425
-in our basement rec room.
-Aw.

00:18:47.562 --> 00:18:49.283
Guess you'll just
have to make do

00:18:49.285 --> 00:18:50.583
with your crinkled ones.

00:19:23.552 --> 00:19:26.058
Honey, the scattered grain
is delicious.

00:19:26.155 --> 00:19:28.881
-You outdid yourself.
-Well, don't thank me.

00:19:28.916 --> 00:19:30.841
Thank the good people
at Monsanto,

00:19:30.866 --> 00:19:32.883
who make delicious grain
that's packed with

00:19:32.908 --> 00:19:35.100
antidepressants and steroids.

00:19:35.402 --> 00:19:38.118
I'm so glad you decided
to come live with us, Meg.

00:19:38.332 --> 00:19:39.177
Me too.

00:19:39.405 --> 00:19:41.646
But I couldn't help feel
a little sorry for my dad

00:19:41.671 --> 00:19:42.686
at the bowling alley.

00:19:42.763 --> 00:19:44.688
He bowled
with the lane guards up.

00:19:44.745 --> 00:19:46.504
Without the jeopardy
of a gutter ball,

00:19:46.529 --> 00:19:47.713
what is bowling?

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.228
He just has his own way
of doing things.

00:19:50.253 --> 00:19:52.663
-Yeah, the wrong way.
-Honey...

00:19:52.849 --> 00:19:54.775
No, she knows.
That's why she left.

00:19:55.071 --> 00:19:57.662
No. I left
because I love your son,

00:19:57.687 --> 00:19:59.295
not because I hate my dad.

00:19:59.372 --> 00:20:01.522
Meg, either you hate your dad

00:20:01.524 --> 00:20:03.357
or you leave this house.

00:20:04.023 --> 00:20:05.376
An old tomato.

00:20:05.401 --> 00:20:06.659
You're just like him.

00:20:06.865 --> 00:20:07.907
What did you say?

00:20:08.257 --> 00:20:11.182
You're just... like... him.

00:20:17.411 --> 00:20:20.745
Wait, I-I can't hit you.
You're a girl.

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:44.841
Oh, Meg, I'm so happy
you realized

00:20:44.917 --> 00:20:47.510
your place is here at home
with your father.

00:20:47.587 --> 00:20:48.919
It really wasn't that.

00:20:48.996 --> 00:20:50.855
It's just...
all my stuff is here.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:51.804
What stuff?!

00:20:51.999 --> 00:20:53.850
Also, turns out Nugget's gay.

00:20:54.023 --> 00:20:56.043
I saw his texts
and it's all tiny cocks.

00:20:59.332 --> 00:21:00.632
Oh, "Nugget" Nugget?